+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard
+**Date**: 2026-08-11
+**Total Epics**: 3 (E000 plus 2 product epics)
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 9–13
+
+---
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```
+E000 Developer Infrastructure
+  ↓
+E001 Reviewed Actions and Workspace Isolation
+  ↓
+E002 Reminder Delivery and Status
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### MVP Epics (Must Have)
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Reviewed Actions and Workspace Isolation
+- E002: Reminder Delivery and Status
+
+### Enhancement Epics (Should Have)
+
+- None in the four-week pilot plan.
+
+### Future Epics (Nice to Have)
+
+- None are planned. Meeting recording, calendar replacement, and autonomous outbound messaging remain non-goals.
+
+---
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic gives the two-engineer pilot a repeatable way to build and test the Python API and browser UI, so every later claim can be backed by executable evidence.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Establish project-local linting, test execution, build verification, environment configuration, and a minimal CI path. It also establishes the test seams needed for the evidence-contract path and the real-role workspace-isolation probe; it does not implement product workflow.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A developer can run lint, tests, and build checks locally through documented commands.
+- [ ] CI runs the same baseline checks on changes.
+- [ ] Configuration keeps reminder-provider credentials out of source control.
+- [ ] The project can support end-to-end and real-role negative probes without relying on mocks as final proof.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Python API and browser UI project baseline
+- Test, lint, and build commands
+- CI and environment configuration
+- Observability/test fixtures for the pilot path
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: None
+- **Enables**: E001 and E002
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: —
+- Models/Services: application bootstrap; test configuration; provider configuration interface
+- Files/Components: CI workflow; API and browser application scaffolding; environment example; test and lint configuration
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3–4
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+---
+
+### E001: Reviewed Actions and Workspace Isolation
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables meeting facilitators to turn an uploaded transcript into explicitly confirmed, workspace-private actions, reducing the chance that follow-up stays vague, unowned, or overdue.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Implement PRM-001, PRM-002, and PRM-004: transcript upload, proposed action items, facilitator review and correction, the text/owner/due-date confirmation gate, and workspace-scoped transcript/action access. It deliberately stops before reminder delivery, which belongs to E002.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] A facilitator can upload a transcript and review associated proposed action items.
+- [ ] An item cannot be scheduled unless text, owner, and due date were explicitly confirmed.
+- [ ] The UI visibly distinguishes proposals from confirmed actions.
+- [ ] A real request-role negative probe cannot read another workspace’s transcripts or actions.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Workspace/request context and scoped transcript upload
+- Action-item proposal extraction from uploaded transcripts
+- Facilitator review, correction, and explicit confirmation
+- Workspace-isolation enforcement and negative-probe evidence
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000
+- **Enables**: E002
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: workspace-scoped transcripts; proposed action items; confirmed actions
+- Models/Services: transcript ingestion; action proposal extraction; confirmation gate; workspace authorization
+- Files/Components: transcript upload screen; action review/confirmation UI; workspace-scoped API routes; isolation tests
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 4–6
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP Critical
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+---
+
+### E002: Reminder Delivery and Status
+
+**Value Statement**: This epic enables facilitators to complete the reviewed-action workflow by scheduling one reminder through a configurable provider and seeing whether delivery succeeded.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Implement PRM-003 on top of confirmed actions: select/configure a provider at implementation time, send one reminder only after confirmation, and expose delivery status. It does not add recurring reminders, calendar replacement, or autonomous sends.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] Only a confirmed action can initiate reminder delivery.
+- [ ] One reminder is sent through the configured provider adapter.
+- [ ] Delivery status is retained and visible to the facilitator.
+- [ ] The upload-to-confirmation-to-delivery runtime path can be exercised end to end.
+
+**User Stories Summary**:
+
+- Configurable reminder-provider adapter and secure configuration
+- Schedule/send a single reminder for a confirmed action
+- Persist and display delivery status
+- End-to-end evidence path and failure-status handling
+
+**Dependencies**:
+
+- **Depends On**: E000, E001
+- **Enables**: Pilot completion
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+
+- Migrations: reminder delivery records linked to confirmed actions
+- Models/Services: reminder provider adapter; delivery scheduler; delivery-status service
+- Files/Components: reminder configuration; confirmed-action delivery status UI; delivery API routes; end-to-end tests
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 2–3
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP Critical
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+---
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+### Phase 0: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Goal**: make the two-engineer pilot buildable and testable before product workflow work begins.
+
+**Epic**: E000 — Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Success Gate**: local lint, test, and build commands exist; CI runs baseline checks; configuration is safe to use in development.
+
+### Phase 1: Reviewed Actions
+
+**Goal**: let a facilitator produce a confirmed, workspace-private action from an uploaded transcript.
+
+**Epic**: E001 — Reviewed Actions and Workspace Isolation
+
+**Success Gate**: the confirmation gate and real-role cross-workspace denial can be demonstrated.
+
+### Phase 2: Reminder Completion
+
+**Goal**: finish the pilot’s end-to-end value path.
+
+**Epic**: E002 — Reminder Delivery and Status
+
+**Success Gate**: upload → confirmation → one reminder → visible delivery status can be exercised end to end.
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Inadequate test baseline makes later proof impractical | Establish executable checks and evidence seams before feature work |
+| E001 | AI proposals or access controls create unsafe commitments | Explicit confirmation gate plus real request-role isolation probe |
+| E002 | Provider choice or failure obscures reminder state | Configurable adapter and persisted visible delivery status |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|---|---|---:|---|
+| E000 | Baseline checks runnable locally and in CI | 100% of defined checks | CI and local command output |
+| E001 | Proposed action items reviewed | 80% | Proposal/review records |
+| E001 | Cross-workspace negative probe denial | 100% of release probes | Real request-role evidence |
+| E002 | Confirmed reminder attempts with status | 100% | Delivery records |
+| E002 | Pilot teams | 5 | Workspace/pilot roster |
+
+## Epic Concurrency Waves & Rebase Cadence
+
+This Build-level plan contains three epics, so concurrency waves are not required. The dependencies are deliberately serial: E001 needs E000’s baseline, and E002 needs confirmed actions from E001. No parallel-worktree claim is made.
+
+## Notes
+
+- Epic boundaries preserve the product contract: E001 owns proposals, confirmation, and isolation; E002 owns delivery after confirmation.
+- Story counts are intentionally small for the four-week, two-engineer pilot and will be refined during `/epic-specify`.
+- No architecture, UX strategy, market research, provider decision, or implementation validation is claimed by this phase.
